{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nThe configured `/mcp` endpoint can return persistent HTTP 502 after concurrent gate load if the\nlive MCP container dies while nginx's single-server upstream still points at that port. Parent\n`witted-invisible-roan` fixed detection/retention enough that autodeploy no longer removes the\ncrashed live backend, but it can still leave recovery to Docker/humans.\n\n## RCA / design decision\n\nPaired load-side work `enduring-ironclad-arrowana` (3499) is already implemented/submitted and\nremoved the largest measured retained-memory multiplier: retained plan-review snapshot state fell\nfrom 256,646,460 bytes to 37,046 bytes on a 9,081-ticket store. This ticket handles the serving-path\nresidue: a dead container can remain the nginx target.\n\nSelected prevention: in-place live-backend restart on every autodeploy tick, before source-change\ndeploy decisions. If the upstream port belongs to a managed MCP container that is not running,\nautodeploy must emit the existing countable `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`/`mcp-live-backend-down` marker, run\n`docker start <live-container>`, keep the nginx include byte-identical, require the same `/health`,\nstore-readiness, and startup-handshake contract as normal promotion, then emit\n`AUTODEPLOY_MCP_SELF_HEAL` on success and clear MCP backoff. On failed start/readiness it keeps the\ncontainer/upstream identity intact, records MCP backoff, and retries on a later tick.\n\nRejected alternatives: blue/green self-heal adds a second MCP process under the same memory pressure\nand risks name/port collisions; nginx passive failover needs an already-live spare backend; Docker\n`--restart always` is already present but passive and not tied to readiness or operator-visible\nrecovery evidence; instance sizing/off-box gates are deferred to `inherited-americium-porpoise`.\n\n## Testing / verification plan\n\n- RED test in `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`: no source change pending, nginx\n  points at an exited managed MCP backend, autodeploy runs `docker start` for that exact container,\n  leaves the upstream unchanged, emits `AUTODEPLOY_MCP_SELF_HEAL`, and returns success after\n  readiness passes.\n- RED test for failure: `docker start` or readiness fails; the dead live backend is not removed,\n  upstream remains unchanged, existing `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR ... mcp-live-backend-down` is emitted, MCP\n  backoff is recorded, and the next tick is retryable.\n- Run `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest -q tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py`\n  and full `make verify` before push.\n- Live check after merge: exercise the tick or inspect logs/health to confirm `/mcp` is healthy and\n  no persistent 502 remains. No Terraform apply is required because the alarm path reuses existing\n  `AUTODEPLOY_ERROR`/deploy_errors wiring.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The selected design is recorded with why alternatives were accepted/rejected.\n- [ ] A reproduced or simulated MCP backend death under gate-like load recovers without a persistent nginx 502.\n- [ ] The prevention is covered by tests through the relevant surface(s) and by an operator-visible metric/log/alarm.\n- [ ] Any capacity/concurrency number used by the prevention cites measured data, including or linking the AC5 campaign split to `inherited-americium-porpoise`."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788837332187960001,"uuid":"cce1831f-8462-4147-869f-0ef64fb91ae4"}